  "original": "My card, the Docix, found in the depth of the Terrarian Wood is by far one of the most eccentirc characters in our collection. Out of the thrity different moves and traits, it has the weirdest combination. \n\nThe Docix was introduced to the world centuries ago. A cross between the Docafon and the Egorfix, both extremly powerful characters. The Docafon's move set consists of the moves Guardian's Oracle and Toxic Monsoon. Guardians's Oracle is a move that helps allies predict where opponents are going to move and place more defense in that spot. If the Docafon has this move it is better placed in the middle of the deck as a support character. Meanwhile, the other variant of Docafon is the one that has the move Toxic Monsoon. This move sends a barrage of toxic chemicals to spray the enemy down. The Egorfix has the moves, Blessing of the forest and Enraged Wildfire. Blessing of the forest is a powerful moves often saving the team in the nick of time. It Stomps down on the lush grass and gathers all the insects and animals in the forest to counter opponent's attacks. Enraged Wildfire creates a strong defense that is best suited for a balanced deck. It pairs well with any move and is almost as good as Blessing of the forest. \n\nThe Docix's move set consists of all four of these moves an while the defense move is useless against a Gofandoyle or a Teraxing it counters those by using its Dodge move which is unique to the Docix. When you don't have enough time to react, it is crucial to be able to dodge your opponent's attack. While moves like Swerve or Dash have a chance of dodging, the Docix's 'Dodge' has a guaranteed dodge which is best when you have low HP and need to save some time to heal. \n\nI came up with this character because it shows how powerful we can be when we apply our skills to the maximum potential. The Docix uses its ancestor's moves with pride which pushes it skills to the max. This leads to it gaining XP quicker than other characters which leads to an overall faster progression",
